213-         William Golding described in Lord of the Flies the kind of society boys might create if left to themselves on
214-a desert island. This is a useful reminder to idealists about children that the kind of society we need to look for is one
215-where children learn to become competent, caring citizens through involvement with competent, caring adults. While
216:there may be many valuable examples of children organizing themselves without adults, these are not always for good
217-causes: the street gangs of Santiago in Chile or Medellin in Colombia are just two current examples. We should not
218-underestimate the importance of adult involvement, not only for the guidance they can offer, but also for the lessons they
219-need to learn.
